'' std/memory's UniquePtr( of T ) (RFC 0018 P4) refuses every copy -- 'dim b = a', 'b = a'
'' (TKO0746), a byval argument and an Array Push of an lvalue (TKO0633) -- and takes
'' 'xs.Push( move( a ) )' on the last line. TKO0746 still spells the instance by its internal
'' key ('uniqueptr<6>'), so only its id and line are asserted.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/move-uniqueptr.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: move-uniqueptr.tiko(10,1): error TKO0746
'' EXPECT-OUT: move-uniqueptr.tiko(11,6): error TKO0633: 'uniqueptr( of long )' needs a constructor or destructor that is not accessible here
'' EXPECT-OUT: move-uniqueptr.tiko(13,10): error TKO0633: 'uniqueptr( of long )' needs a constructor or destructor that is not accessible here
'' EXPECT-OUT: move-uniqueptr.tiko(9,36): error TKO0633: 'b' needs a constructor or destructor that is not accessible here
'' EXPECT-NOT: move-uniqueptr.tiko(14,
